  "description": "2018 BMW 330e (F30 PHEV). J1979 PIDs on 7EB/7E8 and the SME battery ECU (6F1 -> 607, BMW extended address 07), both read on-vehicle 2026-11-08 over the OBD port with an ELM327 v2.2 clone.",
  "provenance": {
    "derivedFrom": "OBDb/BMW-i3s (CC BY-SA 4.0) for the SME DID numbers; F30 layouts corrected from on-vehicle reads",
    "confidence": "v02 (2026-11-08): SME read on-vehicle (captures/bmw_sme_2026-11-08.txt). Cross-checked vs BimmerLink on the same car/day: SOC window bounds (exact), cell V and cell SoC ranges, current, cell temps vs ambient. Same-moment check vs BimmerLink confirms DFA0 bytes 6-11 as the live cell-V triple. NOT ground-truthed: HVBAT_SOH (83 %, i3 layout). Pack voltage: the i3 DID DD68 returns 7F 22 31 on the F30; the F30 pack voltage is DD66 (found by DD00-DDFF sweep, consistent with 80 cells x avg cell V and BimmerLink). v01 -> v02: fixed the request framing (v01's SME reads never worked), DFA0 offsets moved (i3 layout was wrong for F30), DDBC/DDC0/DFA0 gained window/avg/cell-SoC signals. 2026-11-14: HVBAT_CURRENT negated (mul -1). The SME's raw sign is +charge; the app expects +discharge, so drive mode showed REGEN under load and the dashboard would have shown a plug-in charge as discharging.",
    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
  },
  "protocol": {
    "canFormat": "11bit",
    "obdProtocol": 6,
    "note": "SME: tester 6F1, response 607, extended address 07 BEFORE the ISO-TP PCI. Adapter recipe: ATCAF1, ATCEA07, ATFCSH6F1, ATFCSD07300000, ATFCSM1, ATAT0, ATSTFF (see lib/transport/elm327_protocol.dart)."
  },
